[{"id": "R025", "text": "I tap the joint once and listen. I turn the wrench once and leave it beside the slot. I tap the same place twice. I tighten the handle once and leave the slot seated."}, {"id": "R026", "text": "I lean closer, then tap the grease where the crack used to run. I mark the scratched corner with grease, leave the unfinished shaft, and leave the broken rod beside the unfinished edge. If someone else hears it, I keep the scratch on the shaft and mark again."}, {"id": "R027", "text": "I look at the light catch. “Yes,” I say, though the watch ticks. “I think I broke the bracket.” The wrench taps my thigh."}, {"id": "R028", "text": "i leave the repair leg loose and mark the new load with a pencil mark. i leave the old leg still beside it, so the fault returns after the new one settles. if the leg stays tight, i leave the mark again."}, {"id": "R029", "text": "i keep the repair under the floor and tap with my thumbnail. the fault clicks once, so i leave the old part alone. i move the clean part once, then stop when i find a loose screw, a bent staple, or a scratch that makes the old one move. i leave the original repair alone in the fold and fold."}, {"id": "R030", "text": "I put the wrench on the bench and check the bolt against the drawer. “Yes. I mark the bolt with the date and try it under the load. If it still fails, I leave it alone.” I put the wrench back on the bench and wait until the next try."}, {"id": "R031", "text": "you put the repair in the crevice. “not the voice.” you listen. “the weight is wrong.” you put the repair back. the voice stays. the person waits."}, {"id": "R032", "text": "i reach for the spare and wait for the fault to clear. then i photograph the lever and the motor, but i keep the repair in place. sorry—sorry, i’m checking the load instead of writing it down."}, {"id": "R033", "text": "\"Slow. Likely.\" I check the watch. \"One repair. Then wait.\" I place the unfinished blade beside the watch, then place the watch at the same angle."}, {"id": "R034", "text": "i put the tool back and mark the cycle with the fault. “if it works, then the load is fake.” i wait for the next cycle. if the fault stays, i mark the cycle with the same number. “i’ll write the time in the log.” i leave the tool in the wall. “i’ll put the repair in the garage.”"}, {"id": "R035", "text": "i put the repair on the bench and wait for the weight to come back. the fault goes under the load. i put the plate back on the bench. the hand goes down. i leave the plate beside the bench."}, {"id": "R036", "text": "i tap the page edge twice, then lean against the repair. “right here,” i say, and tap the page edge twice against the wood. “the fault spreads.” i lean too far back and tap the wood twice against the page edge, then tap the repair against the scrap. “i write the fault on the scrap.”"}]
